      "summaries": {
        "en": "Nautilus Trader is a high-performance algorithmic trading platform that solves the challenge of building reliable, low-latency trading systems for professionals and researchers. Its technical strength lies in being written primarily in Rust, which provides memory safety and exceptional speed for event-driven backtesting and live trading across multiple asset classes. You can use it to develop custom trading strategies, integrate machine learning models, and test them with realistic market data simulations before deploying to exchanges like crypto, equities, or forex.",
        "zh": "Nautilus Trader 是一个高性能算法交易平台，专为需要构建可靠、低延迟交易系统的开发者和研究人员设计。它采用 Rust 语言编写，通过内存安全和高效的事件驱动架构，实现了跨资产类别（如加密货币、股票、期货）的快速回测和实盘交易。技术亮点在于其模块化设计，允许用户轻松集成自定义策略和机器学习模型，并在模拟环境中验证性能。你可以用它开发自动化交易算法，结合市场数据进行分析，或作为研究工具来测试新的量化交易理念。",
        "es": "Nautilus Trader is a high-performance algorithmic trading platform that solves the challenge of building reliable, low-latency trading systems for professionals and researchers. Its technical strength lies in being written primarily in Rust, which provides memory safety and exceptional speed for event-driven backtesting and live trading across multiple asset classes. You can use it to develop custom trading strategies, integrate machine learning models, and test them with realistic market data simulations before deploying to exchanges like crypto, equities, or forex.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "nautilus_trader stands out for algorithmic-trading-engine, artificial-intelligence, and crypto-trading in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Nautilus Trader is a high-performance algorithmic trading platform that solves the challenge of building reliable, low-latency trading systems for professionals and researchers. Its technical strength lies in being written primarily in Rust, which provides memory safety and exceptional speed for event-driven backtesting and live trading across multiple asset classes. You can use it to develop custom trading strategies, integrate machine learning models, and test them with realistic market data simulations before deploying to exchanges like crypto, equities, or forex.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/nautechsystems/nautilus_trader for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
