      "summaries": {
        "en": "CUPP is a Python-based password profiling tool that generates targeted wordlists for security testing by analyzing common password patterns. It creates personalized dictionaries using information like names, birthdays, and keywords, mimicking how people actually create passwords. Security professionals can use CUPP to test system defenses against realistic attacks, while researchers study password psychology to develop better authentication methods.",
        "zh": "CUPP是一个基于Python的密码分析工具，通过模拟真实用户创建密码的习惯来生成针对性字典，用于安全测试。它收集个人信息如姓名、生日和关键词，组合成符合常见模式的密码列表，比随机暴力破解更贴近实际攻击场景。安全人员可用它评估系统防护能力，研究人员则能分析密码行为模式，为设计更安全的身份验证方案提供参考。",
        "es": "CUPP is a Python-based password profiling tool that generates targeted wordlists for security testing by analyzing common password patterns. It creates personalized dictionaries using information like names, birthdays, and keywords, mimicking how people actually create passwords. Security professionals can use CUPP to test system defenses against realistic attacks, while researchers study password psychology to develop better authentication methods.",
