          "what": "CUPP is a Python-based password profiling tool that generates targeted wordlists for security testing by analyzing common password patterns. It creates personalized dictionaries using information like names, birthdays, and keywords, mimicking how people actually create passwords. Security professionals can use CUPP to test system defenses against realistic attacks, while researchers study password psychology to develop better authentication methods.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/Mebus/cupp for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
