      "summaries": {
        "en": "VoxCPM is an open-source text-to-speech model that generates natural, context-aware speech without requiring voice cloning tokens, making it accessible for applications needing realistic voice synthesis. Its tokenizer-free architecture directly processes raw audio waveforms, enabling more flexible voice adaptation and reducing dependency on extensive training data. Developers can use it via Python to create custom voice interfaces, experiment with voice personalization, or integrate into assistive technologies, offering a practical tool for exploring advanced TTS capabilities.",
        "zh": "VoxCPM 是一个开源文本转语音模型，无需语音克隆标记即可生成自然且上下文感知的语音，适用于需要逼真语音合成的场景。其无分词器架构直接处理原始音频波形，实现了更灵活的语音适配，并降低了对大量训练数据的依赖。开发者可通过 Python 使用该模型创建自定义语音界面、尝试语音个性化或集成到辅助技术中，为探索先进 TTS 功能提供了实用工具。",
        "es": "VoxCPM is an open-source text-to-speech model that generates natural, context-aware speech without requiring voice cloning tokens, making it accessible for applications needing realistic voice synthesis. Its tokenizer-free architecture directly processes raw audio waveforms, enabling more flexible voice adaptation and reducing dependency on extensive training data. Developers can use it via Python to create custom voice interfaces, experiment with voice personalization, or integrate into assistive technologies, offering a practical tool for exploring advanced TTS capabilities.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "VoxCPM stands out for audio, deeplearning, and minicpm in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "VoxCPM is an open-source text-to-speech model that generates natural, context-aware speech without requiring voice cloning tokens, making it accessible for applications needing realistic voice synthesis. Its tokenizer-free architecture directly processes raw audio waveforms, enabling more flexible voice adaptation and reducing dependency on extensive training data. Developers can use it via Python to create custom voice interfaces, experiment with voice personalization, or integrate into assistive technologies, offering a practical tool for exploring advanced TTS capabilities.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/OpenBMB/VoxCPM for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
