      "summaries": {
        "en": "Try is a minimalist shell utility that creates fresh, isolated directories for different tasks or moods, addressing the clutter of scattered project files. It works by generating temporary workspaces with unique names, allowing users to experiment freely without polluting their main directories. You can use it for quick prototyping, testing scripts, or organizing creative workflows by simply running 'try' followed by your activity name, then deleting the directory when done.",
        "zh": "Try 是一个极简的 Shell 工具，专为解决项目文件散乱问题而设计，通过为不同任务或心情创建全新的隔离目录。它采用生成唯一命名临时工作区的方式，让用户能自由实验而不污染主目录，体现了“环境隔离”的实用设计思想。你可以用它快速原型开发、测试脚本或组织创意工作流，只需运行“try”加活动名称即可开始，完成后删除目录即恢复整洁。",
        "es": "Try is a minimalist shell utility that creates fresh, isolated directories for different tasks or moods, addressing the clutter of scattered project files. It works by generating temporary workspaces with unique names, allowing users to experiment freely without polluting their main directories. You can use it for quick prototyping, testing scripts, or organizing creative workflows by simply running 'try' followed by your activity name, then deleting the directory when done.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "try gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Try is a minimalist shell utility that creates fresh, isolated directories for different tasks or moods, addressing the clutter of scattered project files. It works by generating temporary workspaces with unique names, allowing users to experiment freely without polluting their main directories. You can use it for quick prototyping, testing scripts, or organizing creative workflows by simply running 'try' followed by your activity name, then deleting the directory when done.",
